# Build & check (definition of “works”)

When validating that the project is “working” (before saying it works, before handing off, or when asked to check/fix build errors), **use this exact build sequence** and treat any non-zero exit code as a failure that must be fixed:

## Backend

- Run from repo root (there is a solution `.slnx` in the root):

```powershell
dotnet build
```

## Frontend

- Run from repo root:

```powershell
cd ./web/webApp/
npm run build
```

## Preferred way

Prefer using the `build-check` skill (project-local) which defines the canonical commands.
